title: 'pallet-psm: reduce debt by the amount actually burned on redeem'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `redeem` burns the internal asset with `Preservation::Expendable`. When the redeemer is
      left below the internal asset's `min_balance`, `burn_from` also burns that remainder and
      lowers the issuance by more than `effective_internal_net`, while `PsmDebt` only dropped by
      `effective_internal_net`. A plain redeem could therefore leave the issuance below the debt,
      failing the `try_state` check and keeping the debt from ever reaching zero.

      Such a remainder is now sent to the fee destination along with the fee, so `burn_from` burns
      exactly `effective_internal_net`. This matters when the remainder was minted against another
      external asset, since the redeemed pair's debt may not cover it. The debt is reduced by the
      amount `burn_from` returns, and `Redeemed::internal_consumed` reports that amount plus the
      fee.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: patch
